# Upload-only trim for `vercel deploy` from this laptop: the wire died at 28.8 MB of a 115 MB
# payload, and these two image trees are 85 MB of it. A preview built with them absent renders the pages
# that do not reference them -- which is what the Omega check, the demo login and the tutor flows need to
# be tested on. Git deployments are unaffected: Vercel ignores this file when it builds from a commit.
public/designs/
public/images/learning-catalog/

# Third attempt died at 15.4 MB of a 20.6 MB payload, so size alone is not the cause. Dropping the 19 MB
# illustration tree brings the upload to a few hundred KB -- the smallest test of "can this connection
# finish a Vercel upload at all". `public/assets/` holds PNG/JPG artwork only; the Omega check page, the
# demo login and the tutor routes do not fetch it, so its absence does not invalidate what is being
# tested here. A real submission deploy must come from git, with all assets present.
public/assets/
